When the flattering ones come around me they’ll think my heart is light
[G7]Though my heart may break tomorrow, I’ll be all smile [C]tonight
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
And when the room he entered with [F]a bride upon his [C]arm
I [G7]stood and gazed upon him as though he was a [C]charm
And once he smiled upon her as [F]once he’d smiled at [C]me
They [G7]knew not what I suffered, they found no change in [C]me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
And when the dance is over and all have gone to rest
I’ll think of him, dear Mother, the one that I love best
He once did love me dearly and ne’er from me would part
He sought not to deceive me, false friends have changed his heart
{end_of_verse}
